{"step_index":1389,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-25T23:04:33Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-25T18:04:33-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:04:37-05:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-25T18:04:33-05:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-25T18:04:37-05:00\nShowing lines 1-120 of 359\n1: \"\"\"Write output/SPEEDRUN_ROUTING_NOTES.md from mission_order.json, the scan logs and the self-check results.\"\"\"\r\n2: \r\n3: import argparse\r\n4: import json\r\n5: import sys\r\n6: from pathlib import Path\r\n7: \r\n8: from validate_final import check_json, check_mermaid\r\n9: \r\n10: LANGUAGE_TABLE_OFFSETS = [\"0x19be000\", \"0x2458000\", \"0x2f2c000\", \"0x3a0e000\", \"0x44b3000\", \"0x4f8f000\", \"0x5a1a000\",\r\n11:                           \"0x644b000\", \"0x6f5a000\", \"0x7a24000\", \"0x84eb000\", \"0x9041000\", \"0x9b7e000\"]\r\n12: AUTOLAUNCH_MARKERS = (\"AUTOLAUNCH\", \"AUTO-LAUNCH\")\r\n13: \r\n14: INTRO = \"\"\"# Speedrun routing notes: main story, build 1.0.2.1 (Xbox dump)\r\n15: \r\n16: Everything below comes from files in the dump or from the decompiled scripts in `americas_scripts_23_11_2026`.\r\n17: Each claim is marked **observed** (read directly from data or code) or **inferred** (a conclusion drawn from\r\n18: observed facts). Anything not recovered is listed under \"Not recovered\" and is `null` in the JSON.\r\n19: \r\n20: ## What was and was not recovered\r\n21: \r\n22: - **Titles: recovered.** {titled} of {total} entries have their in-game English title.\r\n23: - **Mission order: recovered as stored order.** The game ships its own ordered mission list ({story_count} entries).\r\n24:   The flowchart follows it.\r\n25: - **Prerequisite edges: not recovered.** No data field and no script check was found that gates one mission on\r\n26:   another. `prerequisites`, `unlocks` and `is_bottleneck` are therefore `null`, and the arrows in the flowchart mean\r\n27:   \"next in the game's list\", not \"unlocks\".\r\n28: - **Protagonist per mission: recovered for {protagonist_count} main-story entries** from a required-player property\r\n29:   on the mission trigger records.\r\n30: - **Any% skips: {auto_count} main-story entries and {auto_side_count} side entries** are flagged by the game itself\r\n31:   rather than by playing them.\r\n32: \r\n33: ## Correction to the previous version of these notes\r\n34: \r\n35: The previous notes said that no localized text table exists in the dump and that display titles were unavailable.\r\n36: That was wrong. The earlier extractor only inflated zlib streams that start exactly on a 0x1000 page boundary. The\r\n37: text tables are stored with a 16-byte header in front of the stream (stream at page + 0x10), so they were skipped.\r\n38: The titles quoted from another session for Chapter 1 (Prologue, Gone Fishing, Gear Up, Just a Scratch, Lab Fees and\r\n39: so on) do match the dump's text table.\r\n40: \"\"\"\r\n41: \r\n42: PHASE1 = \"\"\"## Phase 1: titles\r\n43: \r\n44: **Observed**\r\n45: \r\n46: - There is no `GXT2` container. All 24 `.rpf` / `.bin` files (161,307,960,768 bytes) were scanned at every byte\r\n47:   offset for `GXT2` and `2TXG`, and every 16-byte-aligned zlib stream (2,247,302 streams) was inflated far enough to\r\n48:   read its magic. Raw 4-byte hits: 66 (about 75 are expected by chance in that much data), none followed by a\r\n49:   plausible header. Streams starting with the magic: 0. The `.ttpf` files (about 80 GB) were not scanned because the\r\n50:   request named `.rpf` and `.bin`.\r\n51: - The titles are in a different container: a resource whose inflated data carries the magic `0DRP` at offset 0x10.\r\n52:   The English table is `data.rpf` @ 0x19be000 (zlib stream at 0x19be010, 3,866,624 bytes inflated, 36,888 entries).\r\n53:   It is not encrypted. Layout: block table pointer at 0x38, block count at 0x4C; a hash table of 272-byte groups\r\n54:   (16 control bytes, 16 entries of key hash + string index); string pools of NUL-terminated UTF-8.\r\n55: - Keys are joaat hashes of the lowercased text key. The mission title key is the mission ID itself; the recap text\r\n56:   key is `PROG_<ID>_DESC_REPLAY`; the objective text key is `<ID>_DESC`.\r\n57: - Twelve more tables with the same layout sit in `data.rpf` at {languages}\r\n58:   (one per language; only the first was parsed).\r\n59: - The scripts folder holds 749 `.cs` files, a `.csproj` and three runtime files. Its sibling zip holds the same\r\n60:   files. There is no `.ysc`, `.str` or string heap anywhere under `Downloads`, so the 55 `Vm.StringConstant` calls\r\n61:   cannot be resolved. They are not needed for titles.\r\n62: \r\n63: **Entries without a title** ({untitled_count}): {untitled}\r\n64: \"\"\"\r\n65: \r\n66: PHASE2 = \"\"\"## Phase 2: main story versus side strands\r\n67: \r\n68: **Observed**\r\n69: \r\n70: - `<CMissions>` (`common.rpf` @ 0x219000) has 145 `<Item type=\"CMission\">` rows. The only child tags are\r\n71:   `UniqueMissionIndex`, `MissionId`, `Description` and `TextureName`, each with a single `value` attribute. There is\r\n72:   no strand, category, protagonist or next-mission field.\r\n73: - The story list in `story000.rpf` @ 0x3e30b5000 has a type field whose value is joaat(\"mission\") and holds\r\n74:   {story_count} IDs. A second list in the same file ({side_list_count} IDs) holds side content.\r\n75: \r\n76: **Classification used**\r\n77: \r\n78: The split into `main_story_missions` and `side_missions` follows the ID prefix rule from the request. It is not a\r\n79: field in the game data. Result: {main} main-story entries, {side} side entries, {unclassified} entries whose ID name\r\n80: could not be recovered (only a hash is stored), so the rule cannot be applied to them.\r\n81: \r\n82: No side mission was promoted to the main-story chart, because none was proven to be a hard prerequisite.\r\n83: \r\n84: **Main-story IDs left out of the chart** because nothing places them in an order: {unplaced}.\r\n85: `INT_CRED` and `FIN_CONT` exist in `<CMissions>`; `FIN_CONT`'s recap text is \"Return to the game pre-finale and\r\n86: progress toward 100% completion, or start a new game.\" No edge from a finale to `INT_CRED` was found, so none is\r\n87: drawn.\r\n88: \"\"\"\r\n89: \r\n90: PHASE3_HEAD = \"\"\"## Phase 3: order, branches, protagonists, skips\r\n91: \r\n92: ### Flag store (`Virtual.type_37658EE3464E5234`)\r\n93: \r\n94: **Observed.** All 31 call sites were read. `Method_0` adds an ID, `Method_1` tests for an ID. No `Method_1` result\r\n95: gates enabling or launching another mission. The readers are: the \"already added\" test before `Method_0` in three\r\n96: wrappers of `0x947D998BD81F7AC1`, the tests inside `func_10AA55`, and `func_10AD05`. `story000.ysc.cs` has no call\r\n97: to this type. So this store yields no prerequisite edges.\r\n98: \r\n99: ### Auto-flags in `func_10AA55` (controller `0xD2601E252151E04B.ysc.cs`, lines 572807-573097)\r\n100: \r\n101: **Observed.** The function receives a mission ID. For specific IDs it adds other IDs to the flag store.\r\n102: \r\n103: **Inferred.** The function has no direct caller and sits next to the store's add hook, so it most likely runs when\r\n104: the ID is added to the store (mission completion), not when the mission starts. The request described it as\r\n105: \"when the mission starts\"; the code does not show that.\r\n106: \r\n107: {auto_table}\r\n108: \r\n109: **Inferred for routing.** Because the game sets these flags itself, the flagged missions do not have to be played\r\n110: before the triggering mission. They are marked `any_percent_required: false`. Every other mission is `null`\r\n111: (unknown), not `true`: nothing proves that the remaining missions are all mandatory.\r\n112: \r\n113: When the ID is `BIL_FINAL_B` (line 572926) or `BIL_FINALE_M` (line 572935) the function calls\r\n114: `_0x58BECE7D02A750A7(0x4EF9B888, -1, 1, -1)` instead.\r\n115: \"\"\"\r\n116: \r\n117: ORDER_TEXT = \"\"\"### Stored mission order\r\n118: \r\n119: **Observed.** `story000.rpf` @ 0x3e30b5000, list key 0xB95219D4, holds {story_count} IDs in a fixed order.\r\n120: {main_sequence_count} of them are main-story entries by the prefix rule. The replay menu (`data.rpf` @ 0x12010000)\r"}
